On-device AI refers to using AI models that are already trained on specific data, but not needing that data to function. For example, a smartphone with an image recognition model can analyze images from a different location, using the model's pre-trained knowledge without relying on the original data. This allows the model to be used in different contexts, just like a model trained on a dataset can be used to analyze another dataset.

